ProsperoSunshine: a device that can neither join a running stream nor get a capture channel of its own is turned away at /resume

A second device joins a running stream with its dynamic range and gets its picture, or gets the second capture channel
while that is free. One whose Moonlight asked for HDR while both channels run without, or the other way round, was ended
after its stream had started, and Moonlight showed only "error code -1". /resume now refuses it with 409 and a message
Moonlight shows. video::hdr_conflict() comes from the PS5's video_ps5.cpp.

--- a/src/nvhttp.cpp
+++ b/src/nvhttp.cpp
@@ -1571,6 +1571,24 @@
       return;
     }

+#ifdef __SCE__
+    // A device that joins another device's stream gets its picture, unless a capture channel of its own is free. One that
+    // asks for another dynamic range than every running stream while none is free is turned away here, where Moonlight
+    // shows the reason, and not after its stream has started.
+    if (rtsp_stream::session_count_except_cert(last_verified_client_cert) > 0) {
+      const bool wants_hdr = util::from_view(get_arg(args, "hdrMode", "0")) != 0;
+      if (const auto running_hdr = video::hdr_conflict(wants_hdr)) {
+        BOOST_LOG(warning) << "Resume refused: both capture channels run "sv << (*running_hdr ? "in HDR"sv : "without HDR"sv);
+        tree.put("root.resume", 0);
+        tree.put("root.<xmlattr>.status_code", 409);
+        tree.put("root.<xmlattr>.status_message", *running_hdr ?
+          "Another device is streaming in HDR. Turn HDR on in Moonlight to join." :
+          "Another device is streaming without HDR. Turn HDR off in Moonlight to join.");
+        return;
+      }
+    }
+#endif
+
     // Newer Moonlight clients send localAudioPlayMode on /resume too,
     // so we should use it if it's present in the args and there are
     // no active sessions we could be interfering with.
